      ":question/id": "f5ff1da2-5990-572e-a66f-0f449e888e93",
      ":question/problem": "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(2^{x} - 10e^{x})dx$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2^{x}-10\\cdot e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int (2^{x})\\,\\text{d}x-10\\int (e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{2}}-10\\cdot e^{x}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln{2}}-10\\cdot e^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
