      ":question/problem": "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(2e^{x} + 4^{x} - 2x)dx$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4^{x}-2\\cdot x+2\\cdot e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int (4^{x})\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int (x)\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int (e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=\\frac{4^{x}}{2\\cdot \\ln{2}}-x^{2}+2\\cdot e^{x}+C \\\\ &=\\frac{4^{x}}{2\\cdot \\ln{2}}-x^{2}+2\\cdot e^{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
